 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "masses[i] > 0 and speeds[i] != 0 describe asteroid i in a row; a positive speed moves right, a negative one left, and the magnitude is its speed. As in LeetCode 735, only a right-moving asteroid and a left-moving asteroid to its right ever meet, and the nearest such pair meets first; same-direction asteroids never collide. When two meet, the one with the larger momentum mass * |speed| survives unchanged and the other is destroyed; equal momenta destroy both. Return the survivors left to right as [mass, speed] pairs.",
  "provenance": [
